    <outline text="Cirrus vs Cessna">
      <outline text="Cirrus may be a sexy, modern plane, but the biggest problem I am&#10;hearing from other pilots that are looking to buy one is the Cirrus'&#10;longevity.&#10;The Cirrus is a composite airplane. It's value drops over time&#10;whereas the Cessna's does not. I used to fly a 1957 Cessna 182 and&#10;almost none of the major components had been replaced. That won't be&#10;true with a composite plane. I have flown the Katana and the Cirrus&#10;and they are great planes, they just won't stand the test of time as&#10;well. A Cirrus is fun to fly for it's modernness and sexyness, it's&#10;just not an investment. I bagged my last girlfriend with a Cirrus.&#10;Picked her up from work in it for a sunset flight.&#10;Todd"/>
    </outline>
    <outline text="Fly with me Danger podcast [Site &lt;http://joepodcaster.libsyn.com/&gt;]">
